<rml>
<head>
    <title>Your files</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="tokens.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="case.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="mark.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="window.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="frame">
        <div class="case window">

            <div class="lid">
                <div class="head">
                    <div class="mark"></div>
                    <div class="title">Your files</div>
                </div>
                <div class="chrome">
                    <div class="win-btn" id="win-min"><div class="glyph-min"></div></div>
                    <div class="win-btn" id="win-max"><div class="glyph-max"></div></div>
                    <div class="win-btn" id="win-close"><div class="glyph-x"><div class="bar a"></div><div class="bar b"></div></div></div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- The answer to "where is this actually putting things", which is the objection to
                 putting somebody's files anywhere they did not choose. Every row shows the REAL
                 resolved path rather than what it is supposed to be, and opening a row opens that
                 folder in the file browser. The rows are filled by the shell. -->
            <div class="path-line">
                <span class="name">Running</span>
                <span class="datum" id="files-mode">portable</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Every row ends in Open, which appears when the row is under the pointer or has the
                 focus, so the way to open a folder is written on it rather than guessed (the user,
                 2026-09-24: "options to Open each directory"). The whole row opens it too. -->
            <div class="rows" id="files-rows">
                <div class="row" id="frow-0"><span class="label" id="flabel-0"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-0"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-0">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-1"><span class="label" id="flabel-1"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-1"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-1">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-2"><span class="label" id="flabel-2"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-2"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-2">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-3"><span class="label" id="flabel-3"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-3"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-3">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-4"><span class="label" id="flabel-4"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-4"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-4">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-5"><span class="label" id="flabel-5"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-5"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-5">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-6"><span class="label" id="flabel-6"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-6"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-6">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-7"><span class="label" id="flabel-7"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-7"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-7">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-8"><span class="label" id="flabel-8"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-8"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-8">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-9"><span class="label" id="flabel-9"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-9"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-9">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-10"><span class="label" id="flabel-10"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-10"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-10">Open</span></div>
                <div class="row" id="frow-11"><span class="label" id="flabel-11"></span><span class="value" id="fvalue-11"></span><span class="open" id="fopen-11">Open</span></div>
            </div>

            <!-- Two states in one bar. At rest it is Close and Remove everything; once Remove has
                 been pressed the question in the foot changes and so do these, so a destructive
                 action is never one click away and never needs a second window. Both buttons
                 take the focus (the pad and the keyboard walk the rows and then the bar), and
                 both show it and the pointer over them. -->
            <div class="actions">
                <div class="act-btn act-quit" id="files-left" tabindex="auto"><span class="act-label" id="files-left-label">Close</span></div>
                <div class="act-btn act-danger" id="files-right" tabindex="auto"><span class="act-label" id="files-right-label">Remove everything</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="foot">
                <span id="files-foot">Click a row, or its Open, to open that folder</span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
